.TH CLRUCACHE_SIZE 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clrucache_size \- return the number of live entries in the cache
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

size_t clrucache_size(clru_cache cache);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the current number of live (fully initialised, not evicted)
entries in the cache. Placeholder entries created during an in-progress
fetch or set are not counted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cache  Cache handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Number of live entries, or 0 if cache is CLRU_CACHE_INVALID or a
stale (already-destroyed) handle.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
cache is an opaque VALUE handle, resolved through a library-owned
slot table before the underlying cache object is touched; a stale
handle here is an ordinary error, not a fatal one (fatal-on-stale
is reserved for __clrucache_destroy).
Acquires the cache mutex for the duration of the read.
O(1) complexity.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clrucache_capacity (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
